                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7393C73/47: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-31T16:00:00+08:00">December 31, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 2, 1931—2:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Am just informed by representative Commercial Pacific Cable Company that an
                    agreement was signed December 30th with Minister of Communications at Nanking
                    for renewal of landing rights for 14 years from January 1st. Agreement provides
                    for joint control of Shanghai office by company and the Chinese Telegraph
                    Administration, but company retains control of operation of the cable. Company
                    pays an increased rate to Chinese Government. Full details will be worked out
                    later in a formal traffic agreement. Am informed representatives Great Northern
                    and Eastern Extension Telegraph are signing similar agreements at Nanking today.
                    Repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
